## Summary

Problem: The --no-tools flag (Day 77) added all BUILTIN_TOOL_NAMES to disallowed_tools, but:
1. sub_agent and shared_state were added via agent.with_sub_agent() AFTER the disallowed_tools filter, bypassing it
2. MCP/OpenAPI external server connections still happened, adding latency and potentially more tools

Solution:

### `src/agent_builder.rs`
• Added no_tools: bool field to AgentConfig
• Restructured configure_agent(): when no_tools is true, the entire tool pipeline is skipped — no build_tools(), no with_tools(), no `build_sub_agent_tool(), no with_sub_agent()`. This is cleaner than building then filtering, and eliminates the sub_agent/shared_state bypass
• Added 5 new tests: test_no_tools_builds_agent_without_panic, test_no_tools_default_false, `test_no_tools_with_disallowed_tools_builds_ok, test_no_tools_side_agent_builds_ok, test_no_tools_across_providers`

### `src/main.rs`
• Pass config.no_tools through to AgentConfig
• When no_tools is true, skip `connect_external_servers()` entirely (no MCP, no OpenAPI connections)

### Other files
• Updated all AgentConfig construction sites in commands.rs, commands_spawn.rs, dispatch_sub.rs, tools.rs with no_tools: false

Tests: All 88 tests pass, including 10 no_tools-specific tests (6 from Day 77 in cli.rs + 4 new in agent_builder.rs).
